`)}`:""}function wke(e){switch(e){case"16:9":return"cinematic widescreen composition; favor horizontal camera movements (pan, track, dolly) and wide establishing shots";case"9:16":return"vertical/mobile-first composition; keep subject centered, emphasize vertical space, favor vertical camera movements (tilt, crane, push-in/pull-back)";case"1:1":return"balanced symmetrical composition; favor centered framing and orbit shots";case"4:3":return"classic framing; balanced horizontal and vertical composition, suitable for documentary or narrative styles";case"3:4":return"tall portrait framing; emphasize vertical subject movement and upward/downward camera motion";default:return"cinematic composition"}}function kke(e){switch(e){case"product-showcase":return`
## Scene Type: Product Showcase
- Camera: favor slow push-in, static hero shots, smooth orbit for 360° views. Avoid shaky or fast movement.
- Lighting: premium studio lighting, soft highlights, sharp focus on product surface texture.
- Action: product is the absolute center; motion should emphasize form, material, and detail.
- Avoid: motion blur on product, distracting background movement, camera shake.`;case"action-cinematic":return`
## Scene Type: Action / Cinematic
- Camera: high-speed tracking, orbit, whip pan, crane shots. Multiple dynamic movements per segment.
- Pacing: fast cuts implied through camera movement; build tension toward the climax segment.
- Physics: action must obey physics — debris, cloth, water, sparks follow real-world behavior.
- Avoid: static camera for more than 2 seconds, teleporting subjects, inconsistent anatomy.`;case"sci-fi-action":return`
## Scene Type: Sci-Fi Action
- Camera: futuristic tracking shots, holographic POV transitions, push-through-UI effects.
- Style: neon lighting, high contrast, volumetric fog, reflective surfaces, particle effects.
- Action: technology-enhanced motion — speed trails, energy weapons, mech movement.
- Avoid: anachronistic elements, low-tech textures, inconsistent scale.`;case"nature-aerial":return`
## Scene Type: Nature / Aerial
- Camera: buttery-smooth drone movement, wide establishing shots, slow tilts and pans.
- Lighting: golden hour, god-rays, natural atmospheric perspective, true-to-life color.
- Action: nature is the protagonist — wind, water, light changes. Human subjects (if any) should blend harmoniously.
- Avoid: abrupt camera cuts, artificial color grading, motion that feels mechanical or robotic.`;default:return`
## Scene Type: General Cinematic
- Camera: motivated movement — every pan, tilt, or push should serve the narrative.
